{{#extend "layout" showSource=true}}

  {{#content "main"}}
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Recipe &middot; config</p>
    <h1>The folders v2 reads</h1>
    <p>
      v1 shipped two folder keys no module ever read: <code>root</code> and
      <code>static</code>. They were in the defaults, in the docs and in the README, so a
      project could point one somewhere and get silence. v2 removed both.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>This instance's resolved folders</h3>
    <p class="meta">Read straight off <code>kiss.config.folders</code> — the page cannot claim a key the engine does not have.</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>key</th><th>value</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {{#each model.folders}}
        <tr><td><code>{{key}}</code></td><td><code>{{value}}</code></td></tr>
        {{/each}}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="grid">
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Where <code>static</code> went</h3>
      <p>
        Nowhere — it never worked. Static files are copied from
        <code>folders.assets</code>, and <code>.copyAssets(source, target)</code> handles a
        second directory. This site's stylesheet comes from <code>_shared/assets</code> that way.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Where <code>root</code> went</h3>
      <p>
        The only <code>root</code> that matters is per page, not per site: the layout's
        <code>root</code> hash — <code>""</code>, <code>"../"</code>, <code>"../../"</code> —
        set by each page in its <code>extend</code> call, so links work from the dev server and
        straight off the file system. The pages under <code>shelf/</code> set it; this one does not.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>A leftover key is just unread</h3>
      <p>
        <code>resolveFolders</code> spreads user folders in, so a <code>root:</code> left in a
        migrated config passes through untouched and nothing reads it. Delete it — an unread
        key in a config is a lie about what the build does.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
  {{/content}}

  {{#content "demo"}}
  <p>
    Every folder above except <code>build</code>, <code>layouts</code> and <code>assets</code>
    was derived from <code>folders.src</code>. Naming one explicitly beats the derivation,
    which is how this site keeps its own pages, partials and controllers while borrowing the
    layout and the stylesheet from <code>_shared</code>.
  </p>
  {{/content}}

{{/extend}}
